            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0383" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3831: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Lithuania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norem</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaunas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-16T20:00:00+01:00">June 16, 1940—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>112. The Acting President of Lithuania, Merkys, announced in a short talk at 4
                    p.m. today that all necessary steps are being taken to form new government. He
                    urged the people to accept the fact of the military occupation and to return to
                    their normal work. One director of the Lithuanian Foreign Office has been in
                    close touch with our Mission and stated this evening that nothing new was
                    obtainable [at] 8 p.m. this evening although indications are that the results
                    are sad for Lithuania. Evening sessions seem advisable and we may expect some
                    announcements tomorrow morning. Talks are being conducted by Merkys, Bizauskas
                    and certain Cabinet members for Lithuania and Dekanozov, Assistant Soviet
                    Commissar for Foreign Affairs, Posdnyakov, Soviet Minister to Lithuania, and
                    various advisers acting for Russia.</p>
                <pb facs="0384" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>
                <p>One report says that a Russian Commissar may replace Lithuanian Cabinet.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norem</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
